# The update keys HJViewer's apps pin: the public halves of the keys that sign the version policy
# (minimum version and forced updates), and the oldest policy an app built from this commit takes.
# Public values, in this public repository on purpose: client-build.yml reads this file from the
# checked-out source alone, so that no secret or variable of the repository that builds the apps
# can change whom they believe (docs/ci.md, "업데이트 키와 릴리스 기록").
#
#   HJV_UPDATE_PUBKEY=<key id>:<base64>[,<key id>:<base64>]        the signing keys: the current one, the next
#   HJV_UPDATE_ROOT_PUBKEY=<key id>:<base64>[,<key id>:<base64>]   the root keys, two, each kept offline
#   HJV_POLICY_FLOOR=<epoch>:<seq>                                 where the policy stood when this was built
#
# A signing key's id is 1-100, a root key's 101-199, and a key the standard base64 of a 32-byte
# Ed25519 public key: the line `hjv-release keygen` prints is <key id>:<base64>. `hjv-release floor
# --live` prints the floor; it is 1:0 before the first policy. Only the user makes these keys and
# signs with them (tools/hjv-release/README.md); the private halves never come near this repository.
#
# The file is read strictly: each of the three names once, as NAME=value from the first column
# with nothing after the value (no spaces, quotes or `export`); besides them only empty lines and
# lines that start with #; LF line endings.
#
# Both key lines stay empty until the user has made the keys. Apps built from such a file check no
# version policy and behave like 1.5.1; of the build repository's runs only a check build
# (check_only) is made from it, and no run there takes the test keys of this repository.
HJV_UPDATE_PUBKEY=1:vBkBj4sdc4BcHUq4cDQYNE/tetYRdoF9S23/dl/PTt4=,2:+QU4SPfov1UR+p8N6VzRwx1nuRX6Z3Q1J2bwu/eMi7I=
HJV_UPDATE_ROOT_PUBKEY=101:W6DQEEB3tjSsfDyuRcnPV+0pcxDYcmW5t8x+LxoUDYA=,102:WOT4B4OQohTa3XgF0vC4sdtR1Jyl6bJkawnOAOx3y64=
HJV_POLICY_FLOOR=1:0
